154	    /** The clerk limit and floor are shown with two decimals; the clerk limit is null when there is none. The
155	     * terms are the days after its date a claim is due by; each grade's terms are null when it uses the sheet's. The late percent is shown with two decimals. The policy date is null when there is none (the sheet's
156	     * today is used). The period numbering date is null when it is off. The cap is shown with two decimals,
157	     * null when there is none; so is the proof threshold. The grace days are null when they are off. Each of these that carries a figure is the value in force on the sheet's today;
158	     * {@code dated} has, by key, every value recorded for it by from-date. {@code permissions} has, by action, the
159	     * roles that may take it, comma separated, blank for the standing rule. */
160	    public record SettingsView(String clerkLimit, String floor, int terms, Integer termsA, Integer termsB,
161	            Integer termsC, String latePct, String policyDate, String periodNumberingFrom, String cap,
162	            String proofThreshold, Integer graceDays, Map<String, List<DatedView>> dated, Map<String, String> permissions) {
